  "scope": "Two independent author builds reproduce the complete Composer ZIP. Author and build roots are removed before offline installation; unchanged weak and strict callers run before and after moving the complete installed tree, giving four executions per selection. The standalone result-only API projects checked-record payloads through Array and Option results without checked-input metadata. Checked-record native PHP acceptance covers the established top-level Interval, Sized 3 and Bounded 0 101 forms plus the tested acyclic Packet, Holder and Choice forms through Array, List, Option, Product and Except copied positions. Generic, recursive and inherited checked records, other index kinds, open dependent or zero-payload records, callbacks and owned positions remain unreviewed. Both author routes and full/result-only APIs reproduce complete Composer ZIPs from two author roots, remove author and build roots, install offline, and replay unchanged weak and strict callers after relocating each installation. The runs use PHP 8.2.33 and Composer 2.5.5 on Linux x64/glibc 2.36 with an explicit 2.36 package floor, 64-bit machine words and a recorded 20.0 host-load admission ceiling. The archive retains complete packages, receipts, installed closures, execution records and both producer and verifier source closures. Consumer PHP source remains required at runtime. Hosted glibc 2.38 release-floor acceptance remains assigned to the dedicated workflow. Constructor dispatch and peak memory are unmeasured.",
